@startuml Filter User by Admin
actor Admin
participant ": UserManagementPage " as UserManagementPage
participant ": Router " as Router
participant ": AuthController " as AuthController
participant ": AuthService " as AuthService
participant ": UserRepository " as UserRepository
participant ": PaginationService " as PaginationService
database Database

Admin->UserManagementPage: 1. Select filter (Status or Role)
    activate Admin
    activate UserManagementPage

UserManagementPage->UserManagementPage: 2. Update filter state

UserManagementPage->Router: 3. Send GET /api/users?pageNumber={pageNumber}&pageSize={pageSize}&status={status}&role={role}
    deactivate UserManagementPage
    activate Router

Router->AuthController: 4. Route Request to Controller
    deactivate Router
    activate AuthController

AuthController->AuthService: 5. GetAllUsersAsync(paginationRequest)
    deactivate AuthController
    activate AuthService

AuthService->UserRepository: 6. GetQueryable()
    activate UserRepository

UserRepository->Database: 7. Query Users with StudentProfile and TeacherProfile
    activate Database

Database-->UserRepository: 8. Return Users query with relations
    deactivate Database

UserRepository-->AuthService: 9. Return IQueryable<User>
    deactivate UserRepository

AuthService->AuthService: 10. Apply status filter (if provided)
AuthService->AuthService: 11. Apply role filter (if provided)
AuthService->AuthService: 12. Apply search and sort

AuthService->PaginationService: 13. GetPagedResultAsync(query, paginationRequest)
    activate PaginationService

PaginationService->Database: 14. Count total and Apply pagination with filters
    activate Database

Database-->PaginationService: 15. Return filtered and paginated Users with totalCount
    deactivate Database

PaginationService-->AuthService: 16. Return PagedResult<User>
    deactivate PaginationService

AuthService->AuthService: 17. Map to UserDto[]

AuthService-->AuthController: 18. Return PaginationResponseDto<UserDto>
    activate AuthController
    deactivate AuthService

AuthController-->Router: 19. Send Filtered User List Response
    activate Router
    deactivate AuthController

Router-->UserManagementPage: 20. Display Filtered User List
    activate UserManagementPage
    deactivate Router

UserManagementPage->UserManagementPage: 21. Render Filtered User Information

UserManagementPage-->Admin: 22. Show Filtered User List
    deactivate UserManagementPage
    deactivate Admin
@enduml




